course: dictionary
lesson: 6893
title: Overtired
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts. Over- means too much, and tire means to lose your energy. So overtire means to make someone far too tired. «Everyone loses control sometimes, especially when overtired.» Being overtired means you have had far too little rest.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. The sentence says people can lose control when they are overtired, and a meltdown is losing control of your feelings. So overtired must mean tired past the point of coping. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Tired would fit, but overtired shows it is more than tired.
explain: Overtire is a verb, a doing word, and it can change its ending: overtire, overtires, overtired, overtiring. Overtired is the more common everyday word, and it describes a person who has been pushed too far by tiredness.
fact: Overtire means to make someone, or yourself, far too tired.
fact: «Overtired» means far too tired, so you may feel grumpy or unwell.
fact: An overtired child often cries and finds it harder to fall asleep.
fact: Rest is important for everyone, and health and PE lessons talk about it.
fact: Overtire is a verb, but overtired is much more common in everyday talk.
exercise: What does overtire mean? | To make a room much bigger | To make someone very happy | *To make someone far too tired | To wash something very carefully
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Everyone loses control sometimes, especially when overtired» that describes someone who is far too tired. | *overtired | sometimes | Everyone | control
exercise: Ahmed says overtired is just another word for tired. What is the difference? | Overtired means awake all night | They mean exactly the same, so there is no difference | *Overtired means tired past the point of coping, so you may get grumpy | Overtired is a name for a bed
test: What does a meltdown mean in «Everyone loses control sometimes… a meltdown is losing control of your feelings»? | A simple sorry | Sleeping very deeply | *Losing control of your feelings | Getting a brand new toy
test: Which sentence uses overtire as a verb, an action? | Overtired is a common word. | The overtired child rubbed her eyes. | An overtired baby needs quiet. | *Late nights can overtire a young child.
exam: Why might a parent say, «Bedtime now, you look overtired»? | Because it is a holiday treat | Because overtired means very hungry | Because overtired means very happy | *Because too little rest can make a child grumpy or unwell
